  6310.8 ? outLamp1=on outLamp2=on outLamp3=on outLamp4=on outLamp5=off outLamp6=off  "Enter the number which you just recorded in the slide switches and shift left one bit. The output lights now show 11100. The low order bit of the multiplier is 0, so it is not necessary to add anything more into the accumulator. The binary output lights now show the final result: 11100 or 60. 110 X 1010 = 111100 or 6 X 10 = 60 | ERRATA: page 82: Note that decimal 60 is 111100 in binary. It is written incorrectly in two places."
